# Release channel (testing vs LIVE)

Project Intelligence has a **personal testing** copy and **LIVE production** GitHub apps. They are not interchangeable.

## Channels

| Channel | Role |
|---------|------|
| **Project Intelligence ADMIN** (private GitHub `eXtreameGamer2/project-intelligence-admin`) | Personal Admin build for developer testing only |
| **LIVE Local** (`project-intelligence-desktop` on GitHub) | Production Local app / public installer releases |
| **LIVE Cloud** (`centralized-project-intelligence-dashboard` on GitHub) | Production Cloud app |

ADMIN is **not** a replacement for LIVE Local or Cloud.

## Required gate

Whenever the user asks to **commit**, **push**, **publish a release**, or **update the installer**:

1. **Stop and ask** which channel: **Testing (ADMIN)** or **LIVE** (Local and/or Cloud).
2. On **Admin** commit/push, also **always ask: Is this a silent update?** and record that flag for the change set.
3. On **LIVE promotion**, carry each change’s **original Admin silent/noted flag** — do not remake the flag.
   - **Silent** Admin work stays silent in production (no patch-note bullets for those items), even if other changes in the same LIVE push are noted.
   - **Noted** Admin work stays noted (patch notes for those items only).
   - Never reclassify silent work as noted just because the production push also includes a noted update.
4. **LIVE Local always gets an updated installer** on production ship: bump version + `npm run release` (or equivalent). Silent-only batches still bump + publish the installer with no patch notes. Do not finish with push-only.
5. Do **not** commit, push, or publish until they confirm channel.
6. Prefer ADMIN first, then LIVE only when explicitly asked.
7. After a **LIVE** publish succeeds, follow `live-code-scanning-triage.mdc`: sync GitHub Code Scanning from Admin `docs/security-codeql-triage.md` (dismiss + note only diagnosed items; leave undiagnosed alone).

## Do not

- Push testing-only work to LIVE repos without confirmation
- Treat ADMIN as the production installer feed
- Copy silent Admin-only patch details into LIVE/Cloud patch notes
- Skip the LIVE Local installer after a production Local commit/push
- Skip the silent-update question on Admin commit/push
- Skip the channel question because “commit and push” sounded generic
